# Frontend Environment Variables for Production

# Backend API URL
# Replace with your Railway/Render backend URL (no trailing slash)
VITE_API_BASE=https://your-backend-app.up.railway.app

# Google OAuth Client ID (Optional)
# Must match the backend GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
# Get this from Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Notes:
# - All Vite environment variables MUST start with VITE_
# - Never commit the actual .env file with real values to Git
# - Use this template when setting up Vercel/Netlify environment variables
# - VITE_API_BASE should point to your deployed backend URL
# - After deployment, you may need to trigger a rebuild for env vars to take effect
